OpenSSL 4: move Cargo.lock's openssl-sys to 0.9.117 (and openssl to 0.10.81 where locked).

openssl-sys before 0.9.114 panics in its build script on OpenSSL 4 ("This crate is
only compatible with OpenSSL (version 1.1.0, 1.1.1, or 3.x)"); 0.9.114 added 4.x
support. 0.9.117 / 0.10.81 is the pair Arch Linux pins for its OpenSSL 4 rebuild
(cargo update -p openssl-sys --precise 0.9.117; -p openssl --precise 0.10.81).
Versions and checksums from the crates.io index; openssl 0.10.81 drops its once_cell
dependency. Hand-written: regenerate with `pkgmgr lock-patch` on the next bump.

--- a/Cargo.lock
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -2516,9 +2516,9 @@
 
 [[package]]
 name = "openssl-sys"
-version = "0.9.111"
-source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
-checksum = "82cab2d520aa75e3c58898289429321eb788c3106963d0dc886ec7a5f4adc321"
+version = "0.9.117"
+source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
+checksum = "b47e7e6bb2c38cd930d25a23b40fa52e068c10e85f3e03a7f5ba5aaca5713695"
 dependencies = [
